On supported Python 3.9, GNU longname directory entries can retain their terminal slash. Splitting before rstrip produces an empty component and rejects a valid backup containing a long memory/ or plans/ directory. Confirmed with an ordinary archive round trip entirely in memory. Minimal fix: normalize a permitted terminal directory slash before component validation while retaining traversal and repeated-slash rejection.

